## 🤝 Code of Conduct

### 🗣️ Leadership Behavior Expectations
Managers model the standards they expect from their teams[cite: 13]. This includes:

| Behavior | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Respectful, clear communication** | Use direct language, active listening, and constructive tone during all team interactions[cite: 13]. |
| **Transparency and honesty** | Share context openly, admit when you don't have all the answers, and communicate changes promptly[cite: 13]. |
| **Consistent follow-through** | Honor commitments, stick to agreed-upon check-in schedules, and deliver on promises[cite: 13]. |
| **Accountability for actions and decisions** | Take ownership of team outcomes and model responsibility rather than shifting blame[cite: 13]. |
| **Protecting psychological safety in all interactions** | Encourage open dialogue, validate questions, and allow room for learning and mistakes[cite: 13]. |

### 🚩 Professional Boundaries
Healthy boundaries create trust and fairness across the team[cite: 13]:

| Boundary | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **No downward gossip** | Refrain from discussing company politics, peer performance, or sensitive operational decisions with direct reports[cite: 13]. |
| **No venting to direct reports** | Keep personal frustrations and high-level stressors between you, your manager, or HR[cite: 13]. |
| **No favoritism** | Treat all team members fairly, using uniform criteria for evaluation and task distribution[cite: 13]. |
| **No blurred friendships** | Maintain a clear professional boundary while staying warm and approachable[cite: 13]. |
| **No inconsistent standards** | Apply performance metrics, rules, and expectations equally across the entire team[cite: 13]. |

### ⏰ Attendance & Reliability

| Expectation | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Arrive prepared and on time** | Be ready for scheduled 1:1s, team check-ins, and group syncs with an agenda[cite: 13]. |
| **Communicate delays or absences early** | Notify affected team members as soon as possible if schedule adjustments occur[cite: 13]. |
| **Honor commitments and deadlines** | Track promises made during check-ins and consistently follow up on time[cite: 13]. |

### ⚖️ Conflicts of Interest

| Requirement | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Disclose potential conflicts immediately** | Report personal or financial ties that could impact objective decision-making to HR or leadership[cite: 14]. |
| **Avoid situations that compromise fairness or objectivity** | Step back from hiring, evaluating, or assigning tasks where personal bias exists[cite: 14]. |

