## 📋 Policies and Procedures

### 🏖️ Paid Time Off (PTO)

| Item | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Outline how PTO is accrued and requested** | Submit PTO requests through the standard company system as far in advance as possible[cite: 14]. |
| **Clarify approval timelines and blackout periods** | Managers review requests within 48 hours, considering key project deadlines and coverage[cite: 14]. |
| **Reinforce fairness and consistency in granting time off** | Evaluate requests fairly without favoritism while ensuring operational continuity[cite: 14]. |

### 🕒 Work Hours & Flexibility

| Item | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Define core working hours** | Establish primary overlap hours when all team members should be reachable for collaboration[cite: 14]. |
| **Specify expectations for availability** | Keep calendar statuses updated and communicate status changes during working hours[cite: 14]. |
| **Clarify remote-work norms, communication rhythms, and response times** | Set target response windows across chat and email, and establish asynchronous updates to keep projects moving across global time zones[cite: 14]. |

### 📊 Performance & Feedback

| Item | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Managers provide frequent, specific feedback** | Deliver actionable feedback during weekly 1:1s using the Situation-Behavior-Impact (SBI) framework to reinforce strengths and address gaps[cite: 15]. |
| **Quarterly development conversations support growth** | Hold dedicated quarterly check-ins focused exclusively on long-term career pathing, skill building, and stretch assignments[cite: 15]. |
| **Expectations are revisited regularly to prevent ambiguity** | Review individual OKRs and role responsibilities at the start of each quarter to keep goals aligned with evolving business needs[cite: 15]. |

### 💬 Communication Standards

| Item | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Use clear, direct, respectful communication** | State intent clearly, focus on objective facts over emotions, and maintain a professional, supportive tone across all channels[cite: 15]. |
| **Avoid assumptions — ask clarifying questions** | Default to curiosity when requirements are unclear, confirming next steps and expectations in writing to ensure full alignment[cite: 15]. |
| **Maintain transparency whenever possible** | Share context, decisions, and project updates openly across public team channels rather than siloing information in private messages[cite: 15]. |

### ⚠️ Escalation & Issue Resolution

| Item | Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Encourage early communication about concerns** | Address small roadblocks or interpersonal friction immediately to prevent minor issues from escalating into major disruptions[cite: 15]. |
| **Managers guide, coach, and support problem-solving** | Help direct reports navigate challenges through constructive questioning and active listening rather than immediately taking over the task[cite: 15]. |
| **Serious issues follow formal HR channels** | Report cases involving policy violations, harassment, performance action plans, or severe conflicts directly to People Operations/HR[cite: 15]. |

